WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.660
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:22.930 --> 00:28.013
4 CONTESTANTS LEFT. 4 DAYS AND 14 HOURS UNTIL THE GAME ENDS.

3
00:33.316 --> 00:38.623
"Since you continue to act like a fool, I have prepared a new stage for you."

4
00:42.108 --> 00:43.899
A new stage?

5
00:44.941 --> 00:45.736
Why are you here?

6
00:47.024 --> 00:48.650
I've brought you a scoop.

7
00:49.483 --> 00:50.330
A scoop?

8
00:51.191 --> 00:51.723
That's right.

9
00:53.149 --> 00:55.108
That's him!

10
00:57.536 --> 00:59.244
Don't call the cops yet.

11
01:01.774 --> 01:04.316
Let's have a good, long chat.

12
01:17.066 --> 01:18.483
Your face is cut.

13
01:21.233 --> 01:25.649
Police brutality. Another detective with a bad temper.

14
01:28.191 --> 01:29.774
What happened to him?

15
01:31.691 --> 01:32.941
Dunno.

16
01:42.149 --> 01:43.566
What about Saori?

17
01:45.024 --> 01:48.483
Why even ask? Do you think you can save her?

18
01:48.608 --> 01:49.703
Look, you...!

19
01:50.608 --> 01:52.191
You gonna hit me too?

20
01:54.316 --> 01:56.483
The game continues.

21
01:58.688 --> 02:00.688
What's this new stage?

22
02:03.149 --> 02:06.691
I dunno, but we've only got one option...

23
02:07.233 --> 02:11.233
Find the mastermind and rescue everyone.

24
02:12.441 --> 02:13.858
That's right.

25
02:15.108 --> 02:17.636
What happened five years ago?

26
02:18.425 --> 02:20.209
What hospital were you at?

27
02:25.358 --> 02:25.990
This one.

28
02:26.063 --> 02:28.233
TOKYO GENERAL MEDICAL CENTER

29
02:28.490 --> 02:31.210
Tokyo General Medical Center...

30
02:33.894 --> 02:34.852
What about it?

31
02:35.865 --> 02:39.240
No, that's not the one I was thinking of.

32
02:40.073 --> 02:43.198
I thought it might be the hospital

33
02:43.448 --> 02:46.948
from a case I was involved in five years ago.

34
02:47.906 --> 02:49.156
I see.

35
02:51.573 --> 02:56.573
An exclusive interview with a perpetrator of the kiDnap GAME...

36
02:57.448 --> 02:59.448
A true journalist, I see.

37
03:00.323 --> 03:02.615
It'll serve as evidence.

38
03:05.323 --> 03:10.656
Come on, I know you want the scoop. To clear your reputation.

39
03:13.156 --> 03:18.448
You published fake news and ruined your credibility as a journalist.

40
03:19.365 --> 03:23.198
Now's your chance to redeem yourself.

41
03:23.865 --> 03:27.073
Is that why you're working with Niide?

42
03:27.198 --> 03:30.531
Or is it your loyalty to Saori?

43
03:33.034 --> 03:36.992
I'm doing it to find the truth. And to rescue Saori.

44
03:43.031 --> 03:43.865
Let's begin.

45
03:50.531 --> 03:53.365
You're behind the abduction of...

46
03:53.531 --> 03:58.823
"KiDnap GAME." That's more sensational.

47
04:00.073 --> 04:02.281
Was the crime your idea?

48
04:05.823 --> 04:10.531
The game was planned by a nobler, more compassionate person.

49
04:12.365 --> 04:16.781
So you're just a pawn, is that right?

50
04:20.698 --> 04:22.115
I'm ready.

51
04:30.740 --> 04:32.073
I'll be going.

52
04:39.865 --> 04:43.906
I'm following orders... of my own will.

53
04:47.698 --> 04:49.406
What's the "scoop"?

54
04:53.240 --> 04:54.323
This.

55
04:56.156 --> 05:00.865
Broadcast this at 3 PM.

56
05:10.990 --> 05:12.156
What's on it?

57
05:12.573 --> 05:14.448
You'll find out.

58
05:18.781 --> 05:20.698
Can I ask you a favor?

59
05:21.198 --> 05:22.156
What?

60
05:25.605 --> 05:29.143
Five years ago, you and Christina were in Tokyo.

61
05:30.281 --> 05:33.823
Miguel from Manila also once worked in Tokyo.

62
05:34.769 --> 05:35.603
Tokyo?

63
05:35.860 --> 05:37.043
Yeah.

64
05:38.073 --> 05:39.740
Maybe Tokyo's the key.

65
05:54.573 --> 05:58.698
Can I speak to the lead investigator of the kiDnap GAME?

66
05:59.115 --> 06:02.323
Me? I'm the perpetrator.

67
06:03.448 --> 06:04.656
It's the perp.

68
06:05.573 --> 06:07.115
Put them through.

69
06:11.781 --> 06:14.156
This is Samejima.

70
06:19.073 --> 06:21.073
You think we'll accept that?

71
06:21.406 --> 06:22.948
I'll say it again.

72
06:23.073 --> 06:29.073
Remove all travel restrictions on Toshiro Niide and Han Kiju.

73
06:29.656 --> 06:31.323
Who are you?

74
06:31.698 --> 06:35.448
If you refuse, the hostages will die.

75
06:39.198 --> 06:42.281
I have something to offer in return.

76
06:42.990 --> 06:44.531
In return?

77
07:03.452 --> 07:04.151
Who are you?

78
07:08.098 --> 07:09.848
Why are you doing this?

79
07:09.973 --> 07:12.765
Anyone... please!

80
07:13.603 --> 07:14.936
Are there others here, too?

81
07:16.311 --> 07:17.890
Is there anyone there?

82
07:25.436 --> 07:27.645
Please help!

83
07:40.853 --> 07:41.670
Yes?

84
07:42.353 --> 07:45.270
That man you were looking for... He's here.

85
07:46.770 --> 07:48.103
Are you sure?

86
07:48.978 --> 07:51.311
He's inviting you and Han Kiju

87
07:53.853 --> 07:55.811
to the next stage.

88
07:58.436 --> 07:59.978
He wants to meet us?

89
09:06.895 --> 09:09.401
KIDNAP GAME

90
09:15.020 --> 09:17.895
PM 01:32 JST TOKYO

91
09:40.311 --> 09:41.395
Audio coming up.

92
09:41.811 --> 09:45.353
Bringing in the monitor. Check positions.

93
09:45.478 --> 09:46.478
To the right.

94
09:46.968 --> 09:48.051
-Okay. -Thanks.

95
09:48.283 --> 09:50.396
-Be ready to go live. -Okay.

96
09:50.811 --> 09:51.978
Live?

97
09:52.163 --> 09:54.538
If needed. We got the go-ahead.

98
09:54.743 --> 09:57.201
Cut it out. This isn't a show.

99
09:58.136 --> 10:02.776
The moment the man whose wife was taken meets her kidnapper...

100
10:03.145 --> 10:07.710
Isn't it the media's duty to report that?

101
10:16.186 --> 10:20.311
That's why you're going places. You get it.

102
10:21.311 --> 10:24.645
Remember the agreement. Broadcast at 3 PM.

103
10:41.811 --> 10:46.511
Mr. Niide! It's almost time. Any comment?

104
10:46.617 --> 10:47.597
Let us through.

105
10:47.637 --> 10:49.751
How are you feeling?

106
10:49.804 --> 10:50.943
Let us through.

107
10:51.103 --> 10:53.353
Cut that out! Let them through!

108
10:53.544 --> 10:56.416
-Mr. Niide! Just one comment! -Stop it!

109
10:56.555 --> 10:58.847
KIDNAP GAME CONFRONTING THE KIDNAPPER

110
10:59.884 --> 11:01.593
Stay calm, Niide.

111
11:09.185 --> 11:10.164
They're here!

112
11:17.923 --> 11:22.863
Niide. Kiju. So glad you could make it.

113
11:32.250 --> 11:32.922
Stop!

114
11:35.208 --> 11:38.292
One more step and your wife could die.

115
11:40.583 --> 11:41.750
What is this?

116
11:43.537 --> 11:46.329
-Have a seat. -I asked you a question!

117
11:48.787 --> 11:50.162
It's starting.

118
11:50.476 --> 11:52.129
-Are we rolling? -Rolling.

119
11:53.600 --> 11:58.080
Ah yes, angry as ever. Is raging all you can do?

120
11:59.757 --> 12:02.632
No wonder the bodies are piling up.

121
12:03.798 --> 12:05.090
You killed them.

122
12:05.215 --> 12:09.548
Calm down or you'll lose the chance I'm giving you.

123
12:10.048 --> 12:11.223
Chance?

124
12:12.296 --> 12:13.303
What do you mean?

125
12:14.257 --> 12:19.757
I will give a chance to you slaves of desire.

126
12:20.423 --> 12:23.173
That's why I've invited you here.

127
12:30.007 --> 12:33.965
If you can answer my question, the game will end.

128
12:34.965 --> 12:38.798
The hostages might even be freed.

129
12:39.298 --> 12:41.173
Cut the bullshit!

130
12:41.965 --> 12:44.548
What's your goal? Why target us?

131
12:44.897 --> 12:47.981
That's exactly what I was going to ask.

132
12:48.757 --> 12:51.965
Why were you chosen?

133
12:52.090 --> 12:55.673
Figure that out within the time limit and you win.

134
12:57.215 --> 13:01.632
You might even save your beloved wife and daughter.

135
13:01.798 --> 13:04.423
-Saori better be safe... -Hey, hey!

136
13:09.257 --> 13:10.882
What you're saying...

137
13:12.007 --> 13:18.465
is if we figure out why we were chosen, the game ends and the hostages are released.

138
13:20.090 --> 13:24.382
Very good, my dear rational super-doctor!

139
13:25.632 --> 13:29.090
You're buying time while you think.

140
13:29.215 --> 13:34.132
At the same time, you're confirming whether I can speak Korean.

141
13:34.988 --> 13:37.449
So unlike the sinner who only rages.

142
13:40.110 --> 13:43.371
Is the reason related to Tokyo?

143
13:45.424 --> 13:48.630
You'll have to be more specific.

144
13:51.069 --> 13:55.096
By the way, you only get one answer. And the time limit is...

145
13:56.857 --> 13:59.263
Let's see... Five minutes.

146
14:00.027 --> 14:02.023
Well then... Go ahead.

147
14:06.697 --> 14:10.031
Are you gonna listen to this guy, Kiju?

148
14:10.406 --> 14:11.656
Niide.

149
14:16.156 --> 14:17.169
Do you need space?

150
14:18.197 --> 14:22.295
Um... Feel free to use this space up to this line.

151
14:23.572 --> 14:24.705
Five minutes.

152
14:36.364 --> 14:39.850
-Seven participants. -Yeah.

153
14:41.156 --> 14:46.947
Nationality, age, work... Everything differs. But something must connect us.

154
14:47.531 --> 14:49.406
That's why we were chosen.

155
14:53.031 --> 14:53.947
And...?

156
15:03.531 --> 15:09.447
You called us "slaves of desire" just now.

157
15:09.572 --> 15:14.906
I will give a chance to you slaves of desire.

158
15:17.031 --> 15:18.697
You said it before, too.

159
15:18.875 --> 15:23.334
Why did you choose us? What are you trying to achieve?

160
15:23.989 --> 15:27.781
So nosy. Insatiable.

161
15:29.174 --> 15:30.841
You're slaves to desire.

162
15:32.006 --> 15:33.589
Why "desire"?

163
15:36.281 --> 15:40.989
"Desire"... Humans have various desires...

164
15:42.822 --> 15:44.322
Besides that...

165
15:45.114 --> 15:50.531
You often criticize my character.

166
15:50.656 --> 15:55.239
The fact that you're here means that you destroyed our dummy.

167
15:55.783 --> 15:56.866
So predictable.

168
15:57.200 --> 16:01.643
Ah yes, angry as ever. Is raging all you can do?

169
16:03.450 --> 16:06.033
He used the word "sinner," too.

170
16:06.190 --> 16:08.399
So unlike the sinner who only rages.

171
16:17.972 --> 16:19.222
A red rose...

172
16:23.337 --> 16:27.379
There are red rose petals at every crime scene.

173
16:28.254 --> 16:33.296
And with each body. But the number of petals is different.

174
16:35.879 --> 16:40.156
-I had five... You had four... -That's right.

175
16:41.048 --> 16:45.649
Each had a different number, from one to seven.

176
16:47.337 --> 16:48.754
Seven people...

177
16:54.728 --> 16:56.853
The seven deadly sins...

178
16:58.587 --> 17:00.212
The seven deadly sins.

179
17:01.671 --> 17:07.129
Wrath, greed, lust,

180
17:09.004 --> 17:13.837
sloth, pride, gluttony,

181
17:13.962 --> 17:16.630
and envy.

182
17:19.173 --> 17:23.230
Wrath, greed, lust, sloth,

183
17:23.978 --> 17:28.123
pride, gluttony, and envy... Those seven.

184
17:30.553 --> 17:33.603
They're all desires, in a sense.

185
17:34.845 --> 17:37.220
Does one match each player?

186
17:41.712 --> 17:42.921
Manila.

187
17:45.633 --> 17:48.341
I heard he is obsessed with money.

188
17:50.296 --> 17:51.796
He must be "greed."

189
17:52.671 --> 17:54.212
GREED MANILA

190
17:54.921 --> 17:59.837
Christina's adultery must fall under "lust."

191
17:59.962 --> 18:00.837
LUST TAIPEI

192
18:01.796 --> 18:02.712
And Bangkok?

193
18:04.380 --> 18:08.116
Apparently, she used to be dependent on marijuana.

194
18:08.837 --> 18:11.004
That's "gluttony."

195
18:11.129 --> 18:13.504
GLUTTONY BANGKOK

196
18:14.296 --> 18:17.829
"Sloth" must be the cabin attendant in Singapore.

197
18:18.337 --> 18:20.337
SLOTH SINGAPORE

198
18:20.978 --> 18:22.311
Always late.

199
18:22.612 --> 18:25.503
She was even late the night of the kidnapping.

200
18:25.598 --> 18:27.616
SORRY, I'LL BE A BIT LATE...

201
18:28.296 --> 18:31.421
My sin must be... "wrath"...

202
18:31.587 --> 18:34.070
WRATH TOKYO

203
18:34.887 --> 18:40.220
That leaves "pride" and "envy." Which fits you?

204
18:41.422 --> 18:43.172
I don't envy anyone.

205
18:44.468 --> 18:46.389
You don't strike me as prideful.

206
18:47.630 --> 18:53.337
If anything, that fat-cat software engineer in Naha's the proud one.

207
18:54.629 --> 18:59.004
Some might think I avoid surgery out of pride...

208
18:59.296 --> 19:01.212
I don't think that's it.

209
19:10.629 --> 19:11.671
No time.

210
19:12.141 --> 19:16.995
And... It's time.

211
19:17.234 --> 19:21.110
What's your answer?

212
19:31.732 --> 19:35.723
We all committed different sins.

213
19:38.315 --> 19:41.982
And that's why you chose us.

214
19:44.774 --> 19:51.315
Wrath, greed, lust, sloth,

215
19:51.857 --> 19:55.399
pride, gluttony, and envy.

216
19:57.524 --> 20:02.107
We committed the seven deadly sins.

217
20:03.815 --> 20:08.530
That's why you targeted us and made us play this game.

218
20:32.399 --> 20:33.774
Too bad. Incorrect.

219
20:36.149 --> 20:39.149
-Wait. -I said you get one try.

220
20:39.274 --> 20:43.524
What a waste. You squandered your one chance.

221
20:44.690 --> 20:46.524
Your daughter...

222
20:47.440 --> 20:52.607
and your wife must be very disappointed in you.

223
20:58.440 --> 21:02.732
Answer me. Where is Saori? I said where!

224
21:03.065 --> 21:04.440
-Niide. -Let go!

225
21:06.607 --> 21:11.107
If you don't answer, I'll kill you right here.

226
21:15.149 --> 21:19.940
That's it. This is your sin.

227
21:23.649 --> 21:26.274
You let your rage take over

228
21:26.502 --> 21:30.252
and become blind to everything around you.

229
21:33.050 --> 21:36.217
You haven't changed at all.

230
21:49.550 --> 21:53.800
Put your anger aside. Show your kindness...

231
21:54.300 --> 21:58.842
Kindness that shields the weak...

232
21:59.675 --> 22:04.988
That's the right thing to do.

233
22:18.425 --> 22:22.259
Because of you, your wife... Poor thing...

234
22:28.950 --> 22:30.491
Stop it, Niide!

235
22:32.425 --> 22:34.730
-Niide! Stop! -Get off me!

236
22:35.543 --> 22:38.768
-Niide! Niide! -Calm down!

237
22:38.793 --> 22:40.896
-Get off! -Niide!

238
22:43.069 --> 22:45.610
Beating him up won't help.

239
23:00.300 --> 23:03.009
Do you know what a red rose means?

240
23:06.425 --> 23:10.259
"You are the only one. I love you."

241
23:14.675 --> 23:18.342
And what about a black rose?

242
23:29.259 --> 23:32.925
How apt to call this a theatrical crime.

243
23:33.550 --> 23:39.009
All the props are in their places, all the actors in their roles.

244
23:40.231 --> 23:43.795
I'm playing my role till the end.

245
23:48.110 --> 23:52.550
And what is that? What's your role?

246
23:54.009 --> 23:58.092
To hand over the footage containing the big scoop.

247
24:04.717 --> 24:05.967
It's time.

248
24:14.800 --> 24:18.800
This will be shown simultaneously around the world.

249
24:28.390 --> 24:31.973
Five... four... three...

250
24:32.711 --> 24:33.503
two...

251
24:34.128 --> 24:35.253
one...

252
24:35.669 --> 24:36.383
zero.

253
24:36.711 --> 24:37.878
Switch the feed!

254
24:38.586 --> 24:44.616
Breaking news! A wave of simultaneous kidnappings has struck seven cities in Asia!

255
24:45.130 --> 24:48.320
We have what appears to be the manifesto

256
24:48.452 --> 24:50.661
of the chief perpetrator.

257
24:51.040 --> 24:52.753
The manifesto?

258
25:08.779 --> 25:13.529
Humans are beings who feel anguish and endure it.

259
25:14.196 --> 25:20.404
Yet you... you live free of anguish, ignorant of your mistakes.

260
25:21.404 --> 25:24.487
Guilt does not torment you.

261
25:24.612 --> 25:26.737
You are oblivious...

262
25:28.255 --> 25:30.171
It is unforgivable.

263
25:30.450 --> 25:33.317
But I have prepared a fitting penance.

264
25:34.889 --> 25:41.843
If you wish to atone, bring your honor, wealth, prospects, life...

265
25:42.645 --> 25:44.937
and stake them all.

266
25:46.100 --> 25:50.149
I have taken your dearest, most beloved person from you.

267
25:51.065 --> 25:55.316
So how far will you go... to get that person back?

268
25:56.865 --> 25:58.436
What is the kiDnap GAME?

269
25:59.413 --> 26:01.955
It’s a game of crime and punishment.

270
26:02.237 --> 26:06.737
It forces you to see and face your sins of heedless evil,

271
26:07.654 --> 26:11.946
compels you to choose, demands a bitter decision.

272
26:13.279 --> 26:16.696
Humans, who have that spiritual brake called reason,

273
26:17.112 --> 26:20.154
are able to control themselves in daily life.

274
26:20.555 --> 26:24.221
Yet when something dearer than their own lives is at risk,

275
26:24.487 --> 26:26.987
they never think to apply that brake.

276
26:27.612 --> 26:32.404
Rushing forward, they sacrifice everything, even themselves,

277
26:32.946 --> 26:36.029
in a cascading rampage of madness.

278
26:37.904 --> 26:40.696
All humans dwell in a sea of options.

279
26:40.946 --> 26:44.321
Your own decisions are no stranger to folly.

280
26:44.571 --> 26:48.654
The results of these people’s choices will illustrate this.

281
26:48.821 --> 26:52.446
How foolish will people become for the ones they love?

282
26:52.779 --> 26:56.737
By the end of the game, the answer will be clear.

283
27:19.362 --> 27:22.362
Each player has committed a grave sin.

284
27:23.154 --> 27:26.529
They might assume I mean the seven deadly sins.

285
27:26.654 --> 27:28.529
But that is wrong.

286
27:33.237 --> 27:37.612
The players are blindly evil. Utterly guilty.

287
27:40.946 --> 27:42.904
They indulged...

288
27:48.446 --> 27:51.404
in the eight evil thoughts.

289
27:53.529 --> 27:55.862
"Eight evil thoughts"?

290
27:59.237 --> 28:05.737
They're the progenitors of the seven sins, though slightly different.

291
28:14.696 --> 28:16.237
The number of petals.

292
28:17.029 --> 28:18.237
What about them?

293
28:18.946 --> 28:21.571
The number is different each time.

294
28:23.904 --> 28:28.696
They match the weight of each sin of the eight evil thoughts.

295
28:30.279 --> 28:31.321
EVIL THOUGHTS

296
28:31.572 --> 28:33.585
Evil thoughts...?

297
28:35.718 --> 28:38.710
But what are the eight evil thoughts?

298
28:39.710 --> 28:42.654
Our ignorant players shall illustrate.

299
28:46.523 --> 28:50.882
Gluttony: a woman far too hungry for drugs.

300
28:59.737 --> 29:03.612
Hey, next time, text me if you want.

301
29:03.737 --> 29:06.696
I will give you a good price.

302
29:07.112 --> 29:10.862
MAKE BENZ WANG ADMIT AND PUBLICLY CONFESS HIS DRUG SYNDICATE TIES.

303
29:11.404 --> 29:14.987
Lust: an adulterous model.

304
29:19.987 --> 29:21.737
You're not filming again are you?

305
29:22.404 --> 29:24.904
No! And I deleted the old video.

306
29:25.071 --> 29:28.237
EXPOSE THE SEX VIDEO WITH YOUR AFFAIR PARTNER TO THE LIGHT OF DAY

307
29:28.946 --> 29:33.529
Greed: a taxi driver addicted to money.

308
29:41.301 --> 29:44.176
You conned that money from those tourists, didn’t you?

309
29:45.294 --> 29:47.544
Life isn’t all about money.

310
29:47.821 --> 29:50.696
PREPARE 10 MILLION PESOS IN CASH.

311
29:51.218 --> 29:56.585
Wrath: a police detective who rages in the name of justice.

312
30:03.685 --> 30:04.976
Where is she?!

313
30:07.020 --> 30:08.520
Stop it, Niide!

314
30:14.231 --> 30:18.939
Despair: a doctor who ignores lives he could save.

315
30:22.389 --> 30:23.557
Despair?

316
30:29.383 --> 30:31.660
Will she go blind?

317
30:32.577 --> 30:34.183
You said it would succeed...

318
30:36.077 --> 30:38.104
That you'd fix her eyes...

319
30:48.302 --> 30:52.718
Sloth: a flight attendant who’s never on time.

320
30:55.225 --> 30:56.767
Sloth?!

321
31:05.850 --> 31:09.309
-Sorry, the traffic was so bad! -Sit down.

322
31:09.434 --> 31:13.309
CLEAR THE CHECKPOINTS WITHIN THE TIME LIMITS AND REACH THE GOAL.

323
31:14.100 --> 31:20.170
Vanity: an upstart software engineer with a career built on lies.

324
31:21.298 --> 31:22.349
"Upstart"...?

325
31:23.250 --> 31:24.750
How dare you!

326
31:29.350 --> 31:32.267
You're here now! In my world!

327
31:32.850 --> 31:36.184
Do you understand that your son is a world-famous CEO?

328
31:37.684 --> 31:42.684
-That's seven... -Eight evil thoughts?

329
31:43.892 --> 31:45.023
There's one more.

330
31:52.309 --> 31:54.379
And finally, pride.

331
31:57.142 --> 31:58.475
Another player?

332
31:59.392 --> 32:00.600
Who?

333
32:04.350 --> 32:08.550
HONG KONG

334
32:15.225 --> 32:16.836
My client is innocent.

335
32:17.596 --> 32:22.475
There's ample evidence of corruption. The odds are against you.

336
32:22.600 --> 32:27.850
I've always succeeded in spite of the odds. This time is no different.

337
32:31.684 --> 32:34.267
Do you know about the kiDnap GAME?

338
32:37.775 --> 32:41.076
I've heard rumors. What of it?

339
32:41.684 --> 32:44.725
The perpetrator released a manifesto.

340
32:48.267 --> 32:51.600
A heavyweight international lawyer in Hong Kong

341
32:51.934 --> 32:56.142
who wins his cases by any means necessary.

342
33:01.225 --> 33:06.309
Look at this old case, Andy. Isn't it similar to this one?

343
33:08.267 --> 33:10.809
You're right, Sylvia.

344
33:12.225 --> 33:14.392
We can use this. Well done.

345
33:31.350 --> 33:33.142
FLOWER SHOP ATRA

346
33:43.230 --> 33:45.467
This lawyer used his money and influence

347
33:45.492 --> 33:48.447
to suppress the news of his sister’s abduction.

348
33:49.734 --> 33:52.693
A toast to Andy's latest victory!

349
33:53.517 --> 33:55.392
-Thanks. -Cheers.

350
33:56.027 --> 33:57.027
Sorry.

351
34:03.767 --> 34:05.807
YOU HAVE BEEN ENLISTED IN THE KIDNAP GAME.

352
34:08.609 --> 34:11.160
He left the investigation to the police...

353
34:15.950 --> 34:17.683
That's none of your business.

354
34:18.147 --> 34:23.647
Your job is to do everything in your power to locate and rescue her!

355
34:24.023 --> 34:27.956
while working in the shadows to complete his mission.

356
34:29.477 --> 34:32.144
Mr. Wong, isn't this about you?

357
34:32.269 --> 34:35.019
Didn't your sister just pass the bar?

358
34:35.394 --> 34:36.977
Was she kidnapped?

359
34:37.644 --> 34:39.102
Why keep it secret?

360
34:39.602 --> 34:41.091
What's this "mission"?

361
34:41.852 --> 34:44.644
This has nothing to do with me.

362
34:47.935 --> 34:51.310
Sir! Please wait!

363
34:52.894 --> 34:54.566
Why release a manifesto?!

364
34:57.473 --> 35:01.309
Eight evil thoughts. Eight evil players.

365
35:01.977 --> 35:03.343
Five yet remain.

366
35:04.264 --> 35:09.209
Only one shall prevail... the first to complete the assigned mission.

367
35:24.563 --> 35:26.336
Only one shall survive.

368
35:37.314 --> 35:40.814
The hell of my creation continues...

369
35:50.981 --> 35:55.214
Why? Why release a manifesto now?

370
35:56.314 --> 35:59.356
Don't you like being a global celebrity?

371
36:02.523 --> 36:04.606
Is that your goal?

372
36:06.648 --> 36:08.189
To corner us?

373
36:08.314 --> 36:10.564
Niide! That's enough!

374
36:15.023 --> 36:17.398
-We'd like to speak to... -Okay.

375
36:18.023 --> 36:19.481
Excuse me.

376
36:37.773 --> 36:40.274
In exchange for removal of your travel restrictions,

377
36:40.952 --> 36:43.827
he offered to turn himself in.

378
36:46.957 --> 36:50.665
I could easily detain you right now,

379
36:51.606 --> 36:54.189
but it would endanger the hostages.

380
36:56.174 --> 37:01.507
Niide... I need you to cooperate as a police detective.

381
37:06.814 --> 37:10.646
-My mission is to capture the mastermind. -Then you should...

382
37:10.731 --> 37:14.160
Without using the police.

383
37:15.679 --> 37:19.587
DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE FROM STATE AUSHORITIES.

384
37:23.721 --> 37:27.867
Don't forget that you're an officer of the law.

385
37:44.814 --> 37:48.439
Promise me you won't broadcast any of this.

386
37:51.023 --> 37:53.229
Ethically, we can't air it.

387
37:56.439 --> 37:57.773
Pull it.

388
38:04.125 --> 38:05.059
Niide.

389
38:07.231 --> 38:09.689
I have to tell you something.

390
38:10.273 --> 38:12.398
I can't reach Hyodo.

391
38:14.481 --> 38:18.731
That man talked like he'd encountered him...

392
38:18.981 --> 38:21.523
-You don't think... -Stop.

393
38:27.106 --> 38:28.398
Don't go there.

394
38:33.394 --> 38:37.185
Akina, I want you to drop this case.

395
38:38.227 --> 38:40.580
You might get hurt as well.

396
38:40.644 --> 38:43.700
-If that's what it takes... -I'm the target.

397
38:47.644 --> 38:48.473
We're the targets.

398
38:59.394 --> 39:00.644
Goodbye.

399
39:06.560 --> 39:10.144
Can I ask you one last thing?

400
39:13.519 --> 39:15.852
What "sin" did you commit?

401
39:18.685 --> 39:21.227
It's "wrath," for sure...

402
39:23.810 --> 39:28.477
There have been several times when my anger caused trouble.

403
39:31.810 --> 39:33.352
Five years ago, too.

404
39:43.560 --> 39:46.060
I chased a speeder in a rage.

405
40:28.977 --> 40:33.269
The student driving was high. They took him to a hospital.

406
40:35.185 --> 40:36.935
But he didn't survive.

407
40:40.935 --> 40:47.894
You wanted to chase? You wanted to kill him, didncha?

408
40:49.019 --> 40:50.840
Are you happy now?

409
40:51.121 --> 40:53.496
-It's your fault! -You killed him!

410
40:54.288 --> 40:57.079
Why... why?

411
41:01.746 --> 41:06.121
That's why you transferred to Community Safety?

412
41:07.204 --> 41:08.007
Yeah.

413
41:10.871 --> 41:16.704
At the time, all I felt was anger.

414
41:19.538 --> 41:22.371
Out of anger, I chased him...

415
41:24.621 --> 41:25.996
and killed him.

416
41:30.204 --> 41:31.954
It doesn't change.

417
41:35.246 --> 41:36.996
It's always the same.

418
41:39.288 --> 41:41.496
I can't control my anger.

419
41:46.163 --> 41:48.954
I can't do "what's right."

420
41:57.204 --> 42:04.704
Someone like me shouldn't be a detective...

421
42:08.621 --> 42:10.121
I'm not so sure.

422
42:13.788 --> 42:16.788
I think the Toshiro Niide I know

423
42:17.746 --> 42:20.663
needs to stay on as a detective.

424
42:23.496 --> 42:29.746
The Toshiro Niide who's kind to those who are vulnerable can do what's right.

425
42:41.121 --> 42:45.788
Swear to me. That you'll do what's right.

426
42:49.496 --> 42:53.829
Put your anger aside. Show your kindness...

427
42:55.996 --> 43:00.496
Kindness that shields the weak...

428
43:02.788 --> 43:09.871
That's the right thing to do.

429
43:18.329 --> 43:19.579
You're right.

430
43:23.454 --> 43:28.371
I swore I'd never lose control to anger ever again.

431
43:31.829 --> 43:36.954
Akina... We'll take it from here. So you don't need to...

432
43:39.538 --> 43:43.038
If you say not to get involved, I won't.

433
43:43.288 --> 43:48.621
But I'll still continue pursuing the truth.

434
43:52.038 --> 43:53.204
Fine...

435
43:59.971 --> 44:05.627
You said that student who died five years ago was high?

436
44:06.280 --> 44:09.133
Yeah, sky-high on illegal drugs.

437
44:11.907 --> 44:12.831
Marijuana?

438
44:14.153 --> 44:17.496
I can't tell without looking it up.

439
44:20.413 --> 44:22.996
But if so, the woman in Bangkok...

440
44:23.121 --> 44:26.788
Aum was a cannabis-addicted drug dealer.

441
44:27.913 --> 44:29.704
That might be a link.

442
44:40.329 --> 44:42.079
What's this about?

443
44:49.871 --> 44:51.454
Why do this?

444
44:58.927 --> 45:02.327
I HAVE A GIFT FOR MY PLAYERS. VIDEO CONFERENCE IN ONE HOUR.

445
45:02.400 --> 45:04.953
PARTICIPATE OR BE DISQUALIFIED.

446
49:35.480 --> 49:36.280
I'm ready.

447
49:44.823 --> 49:45.536
I'll be going.

448
49:48.755 --> 49:49.736
Ah.

449
49:52.230 --> 49:53.855
A black rose...

450
49:55.564 --> 49:57.314
To me, it looks black.

451
49:59.355 --> 50:04.105
There are many meanings attributed to a black rose.

452
50:08.345 --> 50:09.320
I wonder which one it is.
